<h1><span lang="EN-GB">From Single Plane</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">T</span>his command is accessible from <span lang="EN-GB" class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformations</b></span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&gt; From</b></span> <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Single Plane</b></span>.</p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> The command <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>From Single Plane</b></span> allows the user to establish correspondence between an existing datum plane and one of the co-ordinate system planes.</p>
<p><img src="../images/image3.gif" width="341px" height="191px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Name</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Name for the new transformation. The default name is One plane system N, where N is the number of the subsequent newly created datum alignment.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Plane</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select an existing datum plane from the list.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Co-ordinate</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select the co-ordinate frame plane, which is to be defined. The frames are OXY, OYZ, and OXZ.</p>
<p>When creating the transformation matrix the plane centre is taken as origin and the right-hand rule is applied for the axis order. For example, we select OXY frame. After the transformation is applied, the &#160;X-axis will lay on the plane and will be parallel to its long side (its direction is unpredictable), Y-axis will lay on the plane and will be rotated 90 degrees counter-clockwise to the X-axis, and Z-axis will be orthogonal to the plane and will have the same direction as its normal.</p>
